notes: Wave 1. There is no root GitHub workflow directory. CAW carries its own Actions. The mismatch is advertising CC-01 through CC-15 as if the public GitHub snapshot ran them. The public repository is https://github.com/thePM001/AEP-agent-element-protocol. Document the official run sequence as cargo test -p aep-base-node --lib, cargo test -p aep-base-node --test source_invariants, the scripts/gate-aep28-env runners, the conformance runner and the Docker image. State that GitHub is a public mirror rather than the CI host. workspace package repository points at GitHub as the public repository URL. Dockerfile comment says no npm in the runtime image while the runtime stage still runs npm install. Either drop npm from the runtime stage or drop the false comment so the run example matches the file. Do not add root GitHub Actions unless the operator asks for a public mirror workflow. Do not claim GitHub runs the gate scripts.
acceptance: README has an Official run sequence section naming cargo test for aep-base-node lib, source_invariants, gate-aep28-env scripts, the conformance runner and Docker. README states the public repository URL and that GitHub is a public mirror. No root GitHub workflow directory is added. Dockerfile comment and runtime stage agree about npm. source_invariants or scripts/gate-aep28-env-078.sh fails if README claims GitHub runs CC-01 through CC-15. cargo test -p aep-base-node --lib still passes. nla-policy-scan gate coding-completion and project-completion-bac on AEP-Base-Node crate.
bac: nla-policy-scan gate project-completion-bac /root/NLA-AEP-v2.8-open-source/AEP-Base-Node/crate
